  "body": "Closes #645\nClaim: mac/M1\n\n**Problem.** The reader's top \"…\" menu listed Filtrer and the page items before Hors ligne and Rechercher. Legacy puts Rechercher first and the page items last (`MessagesView.swift:5575-5604` @ 87fe0d1c).\n\n**Cause.** The four secondary items came from three separate `.toolbar` modifiers, and the system orders those outermost first.\n\n**Change.**\n- One `ToolbarContent` (`ReaderOverflowToolbar`) declares the order: Rechercher, Hors ligne, Filtrer, then the page items under a separator.\n- `ReaderSearchFlow` and `ReaderOfflineSave` no longer add toolbar items, and the conditions under which they are offered are unchanged.\n- The offline items live in `ReaderOfflineMenuItems`, so saving a page does not re-run the reader's body.\n- Répondre is not in the overflow: it stays a bottom-bar button, unchanged.\n- A pure builder (`ReaderOverflow.entries`) pins the order.\n\n**Scope.** #645 ships alone: the triage put it in Group R, and mac/M1 decided not to take the whole group. #820 and #821 build on `ReaderOverflowToolbar`.\n\n**Tests.** `ReaderOverflowTests`: 2 tests on the pure builder (the full order, and missing entries keep the order). Full gate green on iPhone and iPad.\n\n**Mac check wanted:** the \"…\" order on iPhone and iPad (Rechercher, Hors ligne, Filtrer, separator, page items).\n\nNo `### Ledger` section: this restores the legacy order and changes no GAP row.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ1auuPWv2FeT7Q4Ps\n",
