   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5) — APPROVE** — head 4ddfd1f1 (branch fix/645-reader-menu-order, before the PR)\n\nThe cause is plausible and the fix fits it: the order seen in #645 (Filtrer, pages, then Hors ligne, Rechercher) matches outermost `.toolbar` first; one `ToolbarContent` lets the declaration order decide, on iPhone and iPad. Checked against the SDK interfaces: `ForEach : ToolbarContent`, `buildEither`, `_ConditionalContent : ToolbarContent`; `let` in the builder; the `ReaderSearchFlow` init and its one caller. Offer conditions unchanged (`isOffered` word for word); search state in `TopicReaderView`'s `@State`, sheet via `sheet(item: $search)`; separator kept; primary items, edit, compose and the #653 suppression unchanged.\n\n1. **minor** — `TopicReaderView.swift:203-205`, `ReaderOfflineSave.swift:30`: `AnyView(Group { … ReaderOfflineSave.menu(saver, …) })` reads `saver.isSaving` in the reader's body, so each page of a multi-page offline save re-runs the whole reader body. Fix: a `View` struct for the offline items, like `ReaderPageMenuItems`.\n2. **minor** — `ReaderOverflowTests.swift`: the tests fail only by not compiling and check the builder's own order. Record a Mac check of the \"…\" order on iPhone and iPad on the PR.\n3. **minor** — process: #645 is in the triage's Group R with #820/#821 (same overflow). Ship alone with the orchestrator's OK, and #820/#821 build on `ReaderOverflowToolbar`.\n4. **nit** — `ReaderOverflowToolbar.swift:3`: the legacy menu starts about :5575 (Répondre sits between Rechercher and the divider); `:4718-4720` lacks `@ 2440d79`.\n5. **nit** — `ReaderOfflineSave.swift:3`, `:45`: doc comments still mention the menu.\n\nNo merge conflict expected with fix/852-reader-bottom-inset (hunks apart).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
